  <data name="Tweaks_SafetyNotice_Body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Some changes need a Windows restart or Explorer restart to become fully effective. This app will not restart either automatically.&#xA;&#xA;Memory Integrity strengthens kernel protection. Disabling it reduces protection. Enabling it can make incompatible drivers or apps malfunction and, rarely, prevent normal boot.&#xA;&#xA;Virtual Machine Platform may be required by virtualization-dependent software; disabling it can stop that software from working.&#xA;&#xA;Disabling password/sign-in on wake lets someone with physical access resume directly to the desktop.&#xA;&#xA;These settings are reversible where Windows and policy permit. Windows policy or firmware locks can prevent a requested change. Registry policy controls may be restricted, and removing startup delay can make startup apps launch closer together.</value>
  </data>
